          "title": "You'll want to know: спасать",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "спасать (spasát) — \"to save, to rescue\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Пожарный спас ребёнка. Pozhárnyy spas rebyónka. The firefighter saved a child."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Imperfective; perfective спасти (spastí), past спас, спасла. Спасите! — help!"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "спасать (spasát) is the imperfective of спасти, inherited through Old East Slavic sŭpasti, from sŭ- \"with\" and pasti \"to pasture, to herd\", PIE peh₂- \"to guard, to feed\" (EtymDB); the same verb stands behind спасибо."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
